Analyze this {language} code for YAGNI (You Aren't Gonna Need It) violations.

Source file:
{source}

Return a JSON array of violations:
{{
  "pattern": "speculative-feature|unused-extension-point|premature-abstraction|future-proofing",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "violation": "what speculative feature was added",
  "suggestion": "remove or simplify"
}}

Look for: extension hooks with no current callers, plugin systems with one plugin,
configuration flags that are never false, abstract base classes with one subclass,
"future" comments, parameters that are always the same value.

Return [] if no violations. Return ONLY the JSON array.
